---
import Docs from "../layouts/Docs.astro";
import { releaseSource } from "../data/navigation";
---

<Docs
  title="Troubleshooting"
  description="Use the operation and error code to decide what to check before sending another request."
  toc={[
    ["startup", "Startup or discovery"],
    ["execution", "Refused execution"],
    ["result", "An incomplete answer or lost task"],
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="startup">Startup or discovery</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>The shell cannot find a command</dt>
    <dd>
      Run <code>uv tool list</code> and <code>uv tool dir --bin</code>. Use the
      executable’s absolute path in a GUI host. Follow uv’s PATH instructions
      for a new shell.
    </dd>
    <dt>Claude Code shows the wrong registration</dt>
    <dd>
      Open it in the registered project, run <code>claude mcp get clink</code>{" "}
      and inspect <code>/mcp</code>. Verify the executable, project path, and
      local versus project registration. Reconnect and call <code>version</code>
      .
    </dd>
    <dt>A manifest fails validation</dt>
    <dd>
      Check JSON, schema version, complete replacements, executable paths, role
      prompt paths and roots in{" "}
      <a href="/configuration/">configuration precedence</a>. Existing project
      definitions can shadow user definitions.
    </dd>
  </dl>
  <h2 id="execution">Refused execution</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>
      <code>path_not_allowed</code>
    </dt>
    <dd>
      Check the canonical directory exists, select the intended CLI and approve
      its folder with <code>clink allow</code>. For project-bound MCP, reproduce
      the binding with <code>--project</code> and restart the server. Generation
      uses its independent binding.
    </dd>
    <dt>
      <code>policy_unverified</code> or unsupported capability
    </dt>
    <dd>
      Compare the exact agent, binary and operation with the{" "}
      <a href="/reference/#admissions">admission table</a>. Installation,
      successful login and native-task availability are independent of
      consultation or generation admission. An agent upgrade can invalidate a
      previously admitted build.
    </dd>
    <dt>Agent undiscoverable, unauthenticated or rate-limited</dt>
    <dd>
      Check the executable seen by the host. For generation, inspect{" "}
      <code>generation-capabilities</code> with an explicit path. Then check the
      native login, requested model and account limits. Discovery itself never
      checks login.
    </dd>
    <dt>
      <code>permission_needed</code>
    </dt>
    <dd>
      Review the project and the native CLI’s headless permission controls. A
      folder grant only approves Clink’s selection of the project.
    </dd>
  </dl>
  <h2 id="result">An incomplete answer or lost task</h2>
  <p>
    For generation, read the exit code, terminal status and{" "}
    <code>side_effects_possible</code>. Save diagnostic codes before retrying.
    For a native task, poll the original handle while the server is running. A
    retained identical request key can recover the original attempt. After
    restart, inspect actual changes or external actions before resubmission.
  </p>
  <p>
    For a workflow conflict, verify the step number, continuation ID and
    original inputs. After expiry, begin a fresh investigation with your saved
    evidence. Report the operation, versions and a minimal synthetic
    reproduction through the{" "}
    <a href="/contributing/#report">issue or security reporting guidance</a>.{" "}
    <a href={releaseSource + "docs/release-evidence.md"}>
      Release verification scope
    </a>
    .
  </p>
</Docs>
